# Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon token.
# Get it from: Cloudflare Dashboard → Web Analytics → your site → Manage site
#
# This token is intentionally PUBLIC — it gets embedded in page HTML so browsers
# can send analytics hits. The risk of leaking it is LOW (worst case: someone
# inflates your pageview count). We still keep it out of git to avoid accidental
# commits and to make rotation easy.
#
# For local dev: copy this file to .env.local and fill in the token.
# For Cloudflare Pages: set PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN in the Pages project settings
# (Settings → Environment variables → Production).
PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN=
